/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186311589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186370330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186396735 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186396755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186396771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186479869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1039 "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution of an Inhomogeneous System" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186228915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229133 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4c4b78fa-76af-5261-87a0-d1960aa0fe04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186229982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186229983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186229984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186229985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Inhomogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186229982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1050 1440.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229257 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ecc6f7d5-a6a0-5418-9648-573635651982" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229982 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186229983 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229982 #edb/ref 1061 589676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229982 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2e2fe55d-42e2-5c03-89a2-e19a648504d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229982 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186230191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229983 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186229984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229983 #edb/ref 1061 589677 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229983 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "77745a11-4271-51f5-b398-2f10162b46cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229983 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229984 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186229985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229984 #edb/ref 1061 589680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229984 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6314ffb3-c936-5a5a-b8eb-f9a041a7e1a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229984 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229985 #edb/ref 1061 589683 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229985 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "96c720fc-5ade-5920-b439-4021bbbc0586" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229985 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230191 #edb/ref 1064 "Matrix exponentials can be used for solving *inhomogeneous systems* of ODEs as well. Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)+\\mathbf{g}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant square matrix, and suppose we are given an initial condition $\\mathbf{x}(t_0)$.\n\nOur goal is to derive the formula for the solution $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ of the system.\n\nFirst, we eliminate the *inhomogeneous term* by a change of variables. We define\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=e^{-A(t-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t)\n$$\n\nand differentiate it using the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(t) & =({e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})})^{′}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}{x}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(-A){e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}(Ax(t)+g(t)) \\\\  & =\\cancel{-A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)}+\\cancel{A{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}x(t)}+{e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{-A(t-{t}_{0})}g(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate both sides from $t_0$ to $t$ and get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)-\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nNext, since $\\mathbf{y}(t_0)=e^{-A(t_0-t_0)}\\mathbf{x}(t_0)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{y}(t)=\\mathbf{x}(t_0)+\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{-A(s-t_0)}\\mathbf{g}(s)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert back to the initial variable $\\mathbf{x}(t).$ To do that we multiply both sides by $e^{A(t-t_0)}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}y(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\ x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}{e}^{-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})-A(s-{t}_{0})}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})+{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to our IVP is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\underbrace{e^{A(t-t_0)} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0)}_{\\text{homogeneous part}} + \\underbrace{\\int_{t_0}^{t} e^{A(t-s)} \\mathbf{g}(s) \\, \\text{d}s}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere the first term represents the solution of the corresponding *homogeneous system*, and the second term gives a particular solution of our *inhomogeneous system*.\n\nLet's see some concrete examples." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230191 #edb/ref 1065 14524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230191 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ff1bfa7f-286f-5481-8170-effabae1aa53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186230191 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306955 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\operatorname{sin}(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}(2t)+3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306955 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186306955 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c139fc5d-402e-5c97-b048-caf60e14b36c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186306955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307958 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186494533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307958 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307958 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307958 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186494533 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186307958 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "8b933995-aeb2-5960-92c8-2edb1a0843a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308718 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308718 #edb/ref 1069 "q-335054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308718 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308718 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-2x(t)+3,\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"180px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308718 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "03656a1f-f3fa-5cdf-b35f-3b5febfaad49" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308718 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+g(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]$ and $g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+g(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as the sum of the homogeneous part and a particular solution:\n\n$$\nx(t)={{{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{homogeneous part}}+{{{\\int }_{{t}_{0}}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s}_{⏟}}_{\\text{particular solution}},\n$$\n\nwhere $x({t}_{0})$ is the initial condition vector. \n\nLet's evaluate each part separately:\n\n- First, we find the homogeneous part. We are given that \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSince the initial conditions are given at $t={t}_{0}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})} & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Notice that \n\n$$\n{e}^{A(t-s)}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{A(t-s)}g(s)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(t-s)) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2(t-s))\\end{aligned}]}_{s=0}^{s=t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+3 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308813 #edb/ref 1080 "applying a change of variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308813 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308813 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08a0e04b-fdf3-54cb-b350-9898e7a963ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309170 #edb/ref 1080 "applying a change of variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309170 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309170 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "373d3c75-9124-5814-aa1b-1a43605c0101" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309173 #edb/ref 1080 "evaluating at $t=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309173 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309173 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "378bdb3a-aeab-5b6c-b752-3f48bb11fc6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309618 #edb/ref 1080 "evaluating at $t=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309618 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186309618 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7045fd1f-3ea6-5e00-83b9-4c746c388351" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1759218630979